# Disha AI backend — local environment configuration template
#
# SETUP
# -----
# 1. Copy this file to .env (only if .env does not already exist):
#      Windows PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#      macOS/Linux:         cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Open .env and replace the placeholder below with your real key.
#    Get a Directions API key from:
#    https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#    Enable only "Directions API" on that key. Never enable Maps SDK for Android
#    on this key — keep client-side and server-side keys separate.
#
# 3. Start the server:  python main.py
#    The application loads .env automatically. No PowerShell export command needed.
#
# IMPORTANT
# ---------
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed, shared, or logged.
# This .env.example file contains only placeholders and is safe to commit.
#
# When deploying to a hosting platform, set DIRECTIONS_API_KEY as a real
# environment variable on that platform instead of using a .env file.
# A variable already present in the OS environment takes precedence over .env.

DIRECTIONS_API_KEY=PASTE_YOUR_DIRECTIONS_API_KEY_HERE
